/*
 * flutter_mitm_stack.js
 *
 * All-in-one Flutter traffic interception for Burp/mitmproxy on physical Android devices.
 * No iptables, no ProxyDroid, no reFlutter required.
 * Tested: Dart 3.4–3.11, arm64, Android 13.
 *
 * What it does
 * ────────────
 *   1. Flutter TLS bypass   — pattern-scan ssl_verify_peer_cert in libflutter.so,
 *                             patch to always return ssl_error_none.
 *   2. connect() redirect   — rewrite every TCP connect to ports 80/443 so it
 *                             hits your proxy instead (Flutter ignores system proxy).
 *   3. safe_device bypass   — optional: multi-layer override for apps using
 *                             xamdesign/safe_device Flutter plugin (MethodChannel +
 *                             RootedCheck class). Set BYPASS_SAFE_DEVICE = true.
 *
 * Setup
 * ─────
 *   1. Edit PROXY_IP below to your machine's LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.100).
 *   2. Burp listener: All Interfaces : PROXY_PORT, "Support invisible proxying" ON.
 *   3. frida -U -f <package> -l flutter_mitm_stack.js --no-pause
 *
 * For x86_64 emulators (redroid, MEmu, Genymotion) use redroid_mitm_stack.js instead.
 *
 * @author   redops
 * @version  1.1.0
